{
  "name": "304. TTS usage header, audio Content-Type and repeated transcription form fields (tts usage header)",
  "description": "TXE-6530, contract C5 and C4. A non-streaming /v1/audio/speech (and /openai/v1/audio/speech) response keeps the audio bytes as its body, labels them with the format actually returned instead of a fixed audio/mpeg, and carries the unified speech usage as JSON in the x-bifrost-usage response header. A character count the vendor reports (MiniMax usage_characters) is no longer overwritten by Bifrost's own code-point count. OpenAI speech requests no longer carry the ElevenLabs-only fields of the shared speech parameters (language_code, with_timestamps and the rest). A transcription form field the caller repeats (include[]) reaches the vendor with every value; OpenAI accepts only one include value (logprobs), so the red half of that change is pinned by the Go handler test on the outgoing form and the case here pins the route end to end.",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "/v1/audio/speech - wav labeled audio/wav, vendor usage in x-bifrost-usage - minimax/speech-2.8-turbo",
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "function bifrostUsage() {",
              "  var raw = pm.response.headers.get('x-bifrost-usage');",
              "  pm.expect(raw, 'no x-bifrost-usage header; headers: ' + JSON.stringify(pm.response.headers.toObject())).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty;",
              "  return JSON.parse(raw);",
              "}",
              "pm.test('audio body, real Content-Type and MiniMax usage in the header', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'failed: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(200);",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.headers.get('Content-Type'), 'content type').to.eql('audio/wav');",
              "  var bytes = pm.response.stream;",
              "  pm.expect(String.fromCharCode(bytes[0], bytes[1], bytes[2], bytes[3]), 'body is not a WAV file').to.eql('RIFF');",
              "  var usage = bifrostUsage();",
              "  pm.expect(usage.billed_characters, 'usage_characters missing from billed_characters: ' + JSON.stringify(usage)).to.be.above(0);",
              "  pm.expect(usage.input_chars, 'input_chars should keep the vendor count: ' + JSON.stringify(usage)).to.eql(usage.billed_characters);",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ],
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"minimax/speech-2.8-turbo\",\n  \"input\": \"Hello from MiniMax through Bifrost.\",\n  \"voice\": \"English_Graceful_Lady\",\n  \"response_format\": \"wav\"\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/audio/speech",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "audio",
            "speech"
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
